# Verification Questions (Answer Sheet)

1. What is the difference between a function parameter and a function argument?
    *  A parameter is the placeholder variable name written when you make a function. An argument is the real value you pass into that function when you run it.

2. How does the this keyword allow an object method to reference properties within the same object?
    *Inside an object's method, this points to that same object so you can read or change its properties using this.propertyName. That way, you do not have to type the object's name inside the method.

3. Why is modularizing code using import and export useful in modern JavaScript development?
    *Using import and export lets you break your code into smaller files so it is easier to read, fix, and reuse. It also makes it clear which file uses what from another file.

4. Why is it important to run git pull origin main before creating new folders and pushing commits to your main repository?
   * Running git pull origin main brings the newest changes from GitHub to your computer before you start. This helps prevent errors and stops you from accidentally overwriting updates already on main.
